{title: Good Christian Men, Rejoice}
{artist: Traditional German carol; tr. John Mason Neale}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Carol}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Good Christian men, re[D]joice
With [G]heart and soul and [C]voice
[G]Give ye heed to [D]what we say
[G]News! News! [C]Jesus Christ is [D]born to[G]day
[G]Ox and ass be[D]fore Him bow
And [G]He is in the [C]manger [D]now
[G]Christ is born to[D]day
[G]Christ is born to[D]day[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Good Christian men, re[D]joice
With [G]heart and soul and [C]voice
[G]Now ye hear of [D]endless bliss
[G]Joy! Joy! [C]Jesus Christ was [D]born for [G]this
[G]He hath opened [D]heaven's door
And [G]we are blest for[C]evermore[D]
[G]Christ was born for [D]this
[G]Christ was born for [D]this[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Good Christian men, re[D]joice
With [G]heart and soul and [C]voice
[G]Now ye need not [D]fear the grave
[G]Peace! Peace! [C]Jesus Christ was [D]born to [G]save
[G]Calls you one and [D]calls you all
To [G]gain His ever[C]lasting [D]hall
[G]Christ was born to [D]save
[G]Christ was born to [D]save[G]
{end_of_verse}
